{"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiregattcontract"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The iPad app and the Mac helper ship separately, so the identifiers and value formats they share live here in one Foundation-only module, and the helper links none of the HID code. HeadwireGATTContract owns the service and characteristic UUIDs, the source mode request the iPad publishes to ask the Mac for a video mode, and the pairing offer and answer that let the helper link pair over an encrypted Bluetooth link with no code. Each value starts with a version byte, and readers ignore bytes they do not know. It does not publish anything or talk to CoreBluetooth; HeadwireHID publishes the services, and the helper reads them.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Identifiers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/GATTContract"],"title":"Identifiers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/SourceModeRequest","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/SourceModeWireError"],"anchor":"Source-mode","title":"Source mode"},{"title":"Pairing","anchor":"Pairing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOffer","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingAnswer","doc:\/\/HeadwireGATTContract\/documentation\/HeadwireGATTContract\/PairingOfferWireError"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The GATT identifiers and characteristic values the iPad publishes and the Mac helper reads.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireGATTContract"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"HeadwireGATTContract","title":"HeadwireGATTContract